<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30207" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mycălē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μυκάλη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A promontory and city in Ionia, opposite the Isle of
				Samos</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2, 223</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 2,
				14, 7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mycălaeus</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to
				Mycale, Mycalean</i>: litora, Claud. in.
				<i><span class="en">Eutr. 2,
			264</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mycă-lensis</span></b> , e, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to
			Mycale</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mons,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 6, 9, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A female poisoner</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 12,
				263</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Herc. Oet. 525</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
